<h1>BB(&alpha;) tree</h1>
<p>
(data structure)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A <a href="binarytree.html"><em>binary tree</em></a> where the <a href="balance.html"><em>balance</em></a> of every subtree,  &rho;(T'), is bounded by &alpha; &le; &rho;(T') &le; 1-&alpha;.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Also known as</strong> weight-balanced tree.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Generalization</strong> (I am a kind of ...)<br>
<a href="binarytree.html"><em>binary tree</em></a>, <a href="balancedtree.html"><em>balanced tree</em></a>.
</p>
<p>
<strong>Specialization</strong> (... is a kind of me.)<br>
<a href="DTree.html"><em>D-tree</em></a>.
</p>
<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="heightBalancedTree.html"><em>height-balanced tree</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
After <strong>Johann Blieberger</strong> &lt;<a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="0d6f6164686f4d6c7879622379787a646863236c6e236c79">[email&#160;protected]</a>&gt;, <em>Discrete Loops and Worst Case Performance</em>, page 22. </p> 
<p> See <a href="../terms.html#GBY91">[GBY91, pages 100-102]</a>.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>
<h2>Implementation</h2>
Worst-case behavior of <a href="https://www.auto.tuwien.ac.at/~blieb/woop/euclid.html" target="_blank">traversal, annotated for real time (WOOP/ADA)</a>, including bibliography. <a href="https://users.dcc.uchile.cl/~rbaeza/handbook/algs/3/3414.ins.c" target="_blank">insert (C and Pascal)</a> and <a href="https://users.dcc.uchile.cl/~rbaeza/handbook/algs/3/3414.del.c" target="_blank">delete (C and Pascal)</a> that use <a href="https://users.dcc.uchile.cl/~rbaeza/handbook/algs/3/3414.chckr.c" target="_blank">check root (C and Pascal)</a> (or <a href="https://users.dcc.uchile.cl/~rbaeza/handbook/algs/3/3415.chckr.c" target="_blank">this one</a> or <a href="https://users.dcc.uchile.cl/~rbaeza/handbook/algs/3/34155.chckr.c" target="_blank">this one</a>?),  <a href="https://users.dcc.uchile.cl/~rbaeza/handbook/algs/3/3414.lrot.c" target="_blank">left rotation (C and Pascal)</a>, and <a href="https://users.dcc.uchile.cl/~rbaeza/handbook/algs/3/3414.rrot.c" target="_blank">right rotation (C and Pascal)</a>.

